"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith=self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith||[]).push([[91548],{491548:e=>{e.exports='---\nname: migration\ndescription: Tableau → Databricks AI/BI migration reference. Use when converting Tableau workbooks (.twb/.twbx) into metric views and AI/BI dashboards — includes mappings for visual types, calculated fields, shelves, and per-step migration tactics.\n---\n\n# Tableau → AI/BI Migration\n\nMigration-specific logic and a routing index to the detailed sub-skills. The system prompt owns the end-to-end workflow (Phase A and Phase B), the architecture, and the DLMV vs UC target selection.\n\n## Coverage at a Glance\n\n| Category      | Coverage                                                                                            | Detail                                                       |\n| ------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Visual types  | Most chart types ✅; treemap, gantt, bullet, word cloud, density ❌                                 | `visuals.md`                                                 |\n| Calculations  | Row-level + aggregates ✅; FIXED/EXCLUDE LOD ⚠️; INCLUDE LOD ❌; table calcs only TOTAL/RUNNING_SUM | `calc_to_sql.md`, `lod_expressions.md`, `window_measures.md` |\n| Filters       | Data-source / dimension / quick / range / date filters ✅; parameter-driven ❌; action filters ❌   | `filters.md`                                                 |\n| Layout        | Worksheets → dashboard pages with grid layout ✅                                                    | `dashboard_build.md`                                         |\n| Parameters    | Skipped (no AI/BI equivalent for parameter-driven calcs or filters)                                 | —                                                            |\n| Data blending | Skipped — entire workbook                                                                           | —                                                            |\n\n## Skip Criteria\n\nApply this decision tree to every calculation:\n\n```\nIF calculation contains [Parameters.XXX]\n  → SKIP: "Parameter reference not supported"\n\nELSE IF calculation is an LOD expression ({FIXED ...}, {INCLUDE ...}, {EXCLUDE ...})\n  → Classify per lod_expressions.md:\n    - INCLUDE         → SKIP\n    - EXCLUDE         → migrate as window measure (range: all)\n    - FIXED / TABLE_SCOPED → migrate via source SQL OVER()\n    - Nested LOD      → apply nested-LOD decision tree\n\nELSE IF calculation contains a table-calculation function\n  → MIGRATE only TOTAL / RUNNING_SUM (see window_measures.md); SKIP all others (RANK, INDEX, LAST, WINDOW_*, etc.)\n\nELSE IF data source uses data blending\n  → SKIP entire workbook: "Data blending not supported"\n\nELSE\n  → Translate per calc_to_sql.md\n```\n\nWhen uncertain about any calculation, SKIP — it\'s the safe default.\n\n## Skip Documentation Format\n\nDocument every skipped item in the metric view\'s top-level `comment:` field (NOT as `#` line comments — UC ignores those). One skipped item per line:\n\n```yaml\ncomment: |\n  Migrated from Tableau workbook "Sales Dashboard".\n  Skipped calculations:\n  - SKIPPED: Date Param Filter; Reason: Parameter reference not supported; Original: [Parameters.Date Choice]\n  - SKIPPED: Avg Customer Sales; Reason: INCLUDE LOD — no Databricks equivalent; Original: AVG({INCLUDE [Customer ID] : SUM([Sales])})\n  - SKIPPED: Sales Rank; Reason: Table calculation not supported; Original: RANK(SUM([Sales]))\n```\n\n## Tableau ↔ AI/BI Conceptual Map\n\n\x3c!-- prettier-ignore --\x3e\n| Concept         | Tableau              | AI/BI                                                              |\n| --------------- | -------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Field reference | `[Field Name]`       | `field_name` (backtick when name has spaces or special chars)      |\n| Aggregation     | Implicit in measures | Explicit `MEASURE(name)` in widget queries; `disaggregated: false` |\n| String concat   | `+` operator         | `CONCAT(...)` or `||`                                              |\n| Null handling   | `ZN()`, `IFNULL()`   | `COALESCE()`                                                       |\n| Conditional     | `IF/THEN/ELSE`       | `CASE/WHEN/ELSE`                                                   |\n| Division safety | None (∞ or null)     | Returns NULL — no `NULLIF` wrapper needed                          |\n\nPer-function translation tables live in `calc_to_sql.md`.\n\n## Files\n\n| File                                               | Use when                                                                                 |\n| -------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| [metadata_extraction.md](metadata_extraction.md)   | Reading the parsed metadata JSON — preferred for almost every Phase A/B question         |\n| [xml_extraction.md](xml_extraction.md)             | Fallback: when a needed attribute isn\'t surfaced in the metadata, query the raw .twb XML |\n| [visuals.md](visuals.md)                           | Picking the AI/BI widget for a Tableau worksheet                                         |\n| [calc_to_sql.md](calc_to_sql.md)                   | Translating a Tableau calculated field to SQL; division safety; value aliases            |\n| [lod_expressions.md](lod_expressions.md)           | Migrating `FIXED` / `INCLUDE` / `EXCLUDE` LODs (decision tree + SOURCE_SQL_OVER pattern) |\n| [window_measures.md](window_measures.md)           | Converting `TOTAL` / `RUNNING_SUM` table calcs to window measures                        |\n| [filters.md](filters.md)                           | Mapping Tableau filters to metric view / widget-scoped / page filter widgets             |\n| [dashboard_build.md](dashboard_build.md)           | Phase B — elements to include when dispatching the dashboard sub-agent                   |\n| [published_datasource.md](published_datasource.md) | Resolving a `sqlproxy` workbook datasource against a companion `.tds`/`.tdsx` file       |\n| [validation.md](validation.md)                     | Phase C — comparing migrated widgets to the original Tableau renders and routing fixes   |\n\nLoad only the file matching your current step.\n'}}]);
